 R←TestSvg;m;b;same;obs;o;sky;run;stmt;fn;before;svg
⍝ PlotSvg and FrameSvg return exactly the SVG that the book's PLOTSVG
⍝ and FRAMESVG return for the same observation; SaveSvg writes it
 m←## ⋄ b←##.Data ⋄ R←1
 same←{(⊃⍵)≡2⊃⍵:1 ⋄ 0⊣⎕←'FAIL: TestSvg: ',⍺}
 run←'STATEDDAYNO←JNU⊃OBS' 'STATEDTIME LAT LONG←1↓OBS'
 run,←'TIME←LONG TIMEADJUST STATEDTIME' 'DATE←STATEDDAYNO+(TIME÷24)-LONG÷360'
 run,←'CALCULATEPLANETS' 'CALCULATESTARS'   ⍝ as EXAMPLE_SVG

⍝ Anaheim 1974; Kohoutek in range; southern hemisphere
 obs←⊂(5 16 1974)5 33.767 ¯117.833
 obs,←⊂(1 10 1974)18 51.5 ¯0.13
 obs,←⊂(12 25 1975)10 ¯33.87 151.21
 before←m.⎕NL ¯2 ¯9
 :For o :In obs
     sky←m.SkyAt(b.JNU⊃o),1↓o
     b.OBS←o
     :For stmt :In run
         b⍎stmt
     :EndFor
     R∧←('PlotSvg ',⍕⊃o)same(m.PlotSvg sky)(b.PLOTSVG)
     R∧←('FrameSvg ',⍕⊃o)same(m.FrameSvg sky)(b.FRAMESVG)
     R∧←('3800 PlotSvg ',⍕⊃o)same(3800 m.PlotSvg sky)(m.FrameSvg sky)
 :EndFor
 b.⎕EX'OBS'

⍝ SaveSvg writes the same file as the book's SAVESVG (book globals are
⍝ still set for the last observation)
 {}3 ⎕MKDIR'output'
 fn←'output/TestSvg_book.svg' 'output/TestSvg_modern.svg'
 b.SAVESVG⊃fn
 (2⊃fn)m.SaveSvg sky
 R∧←'SaveSvg file'same(⊃⎕NGET⊃fn)(⊃⎕NGET 2⊃fn)
 R∧←'SaveSvg content'same(m.PlotSvg sky)(¯1↓⊃⎕NGET 2⊃fn)
 {}⎕NDELETE¨fn
 R∧←'no globals set'same before(m.⎕NL ¯2 ¯9)

 :If R
     ⎕←'PASS: TestSvg (',(⍕≢obs),' observations)'
 :EndIf
